    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-036: Attribute Selectors + `clear` Property** — addresses ADR-035's honest \"partial\" finding: below-fold thumbnails don't float right because their CSS rule uses attribute-token selectors we likely don't parse, and `clear` isn't handled at all.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands in a follow-up PR (Commit 1 diagnostic will settle the exact scope).\n\n## The root cause\n\nWikipedia's thumbnail rule:\n\n```css\nfigure[typeof~='mw:File/Thumb'],\nfigure[typeof~='mw:File/Frame'] {\n    display: table;\n    text-align: center;\n    clear: right;\n    float: right;\n    margin: 0.5em 0 1.3em 1.4em;\n}\n```\n\nTwo blockers:\n\n1. **`[typeof~='mw:File/Thumb']`** — word-token attribute selector. Our cascade likely doesn't parse `[attr~=val]` syntax.\n2. **`clear: right`** — not parsed by layout at all today.\n\n**Tree evidence** (post-ADR-035):\n```\nFOUND IMG as Box x=346 y=6481 w=250 h=250\n  (HTML5 logo — left of content, not right edge)\n```\n\nThe `x=346` is the content-left of some container, not the right edge of a right-float. Cascade coverage gap, not layout bug.\n\n## `clear` distribution in Wikipedia CSS\n\n| Value | Count |\n|---|---|\n| `clear: both` | 7 |\n| `clear: right` | 5 |\n| `clear: none` | 4 |\n| `clear: left` | 3 |\n| `clear: right !important` | 1 |\n\n20 total. Worth full support.\n\n## Honest timing correction\n\nMeasurement now shows **6.3 sec** render (was 5.0–5.5s pre-ADR-035). ADR-035's spec predicted 5.3–5.8s; actual is 6.3s — **~1 second added, 2–3× predicted cost**. Real cost of 8 sync fetches at layout time on cold cache. Corrected in ADR-035's Post-ADR-036 note.\n\n## The decision\n\nTwo coupled fixes shipped together:\n\n### 1. Cascade: attribute selector support\n\nAll seven forms: `[attr]`, `[attr=val]`, `[attr~=val]`, `[attr|=val]`, `[attr^=val]`, `[attr$=val]`, `[attr*=val]`.\n\n~40-60 lines AST + ~30 lines each parse/match. Broadly useful — 16+ rules in Wikipedia CSS use `[role=...]`, `[aria-*]`, `[href]`.\n\n### 2. Layout: `clear` property support\n\n- **On a float**: forces it below prior same-direction floats — consecutive figures stack vertically\n- **On a non-float block**: forces block below active floats — section headings with `clear: both` jump correctly\n\n~30 lines in `layout.cpp` (both float and non-float branches).\n\n**Ships together** because they're coupled: cascade alone floats thumbnails but consecutive floats overlap; layout alone wouldn't help because nothing has `float: right` if the selector doesn't match.\n\n## Expected visible delta (below fold only)\n\n| Element | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| HTML5 logo img x | 346 | **~1422** |\n| Categories img x | 346 | **~1422** |\n| Footer wikimedia x | 67 | **~1550** |\n| Footer mediawiki x | 67 | **~1550** |\n| First viewport | (wordmark, tagline) | **unchanged** |\n\n## Five honest caveats\n\n1. **First viewport unchanged** — thumbnails below fold\n2. **Article body height excludes floats** — no `display: flow-root` support (ADR-037)\n3. **Timing correction for ADR-035** recorded (6.3s not 5.3-5.8s)\n4. **Navbox overlap at x=324 unchanged** — separate defect\n5. **Root cause verified in Commit 1** — if attribute selectors are already supported, scope collapses to clear-only (~40 lines, 3 PRs not 4)\n\n## Structural value\n\nFull attribute selector support opens 16+ rules in Wikipedia CSS (`[role='button']`, `[aria-*]`, `[href]`). `clear` completes the float model (stacking + jump-below). Both are pure cascade+layout; **zero workarounds added**.\n\n## Test plan\n\nCascade (`[css][attr-sel]` tag): 12-15 tests covering all seven forms + compound selector matching + non-match cases.\n\nLayout (`[layout][clear][adr-036]` tag): 6-8 tests covering float stacking, non-float jump-below, `clear: none` flows beside, `clear: both` matches either.\n\n## Verification\n\nPost-implementation visual check on Wikipedia HTML: thumbnail tree shows figure at right edge, following text narrowed but not jumping (matches real Wikipedia); consecutive thumbnails stack; footer SVGs at right.\n\n## What's next\n\nAfter ADR-036:\n- **ADR-037**: `display: flow-root` (article body includes float heights)\n- Small follow-ups: navbox hide, `calc()`, `max-width`, JPEG decode, `object-fit`\n\nRefs #187\n",
